    "created_at": "2017-03-14T02:00:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-14T02:00:59Z",
    "body": "I wouldn't be opposed to implementing something in WebKit.  Right now the URL object can be used to effectively access something like ICU's uidna_name_toASCII from JavaScript, but there's no way to access anything like ICU's uidna_nameToUnicode from JavaScript.  It would be trivial to add, it wouldn't increase browser binary size, but it would greatly reduce content size of projects that really want to do this, like indolering seems to.",
